Two completed feature branches were deleted after being "merged," but their comm
its never reached `origin/main`. A subsequent `git reset --hard origin/main` sil
ently discarded the local merge commits, leaving ~20 hours of work as dangling c
ommits. The root cause was that `git branch -d` only checks if a branch is merge
