ser to provide it manually.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Commands\n    30\t\n    31\t##
# `ship`\n    32\t\n    33\tRun the pre-merge validation gate.\n    34\t\n    35
\t**Procedure:**\n    36\t\n    37\t1. **Sync with main** — pull latest main, at
tempt trivial merge conflict resolution\n    38\t2. **Stacked branch detection**
— run `git merge-base HEAD main` and compare to `git rev-parse main`. If they di
ffer, the branch was not branched directly from main\'s current tip — treat as s
tacked.\n    39\t   - Identify the parent branch by scanning `git log --oneline 
--decorate main..HEAD` for the nearest named ancestor (the last commit decorated
with a non-HEAD, non-remote ref).\n    40\t   - Still create the PR against the 
parent branch — that is correct at creation time.\n    41\t   - Prepend a `⚠️ STA
CKED PR` section to the PR body:\n    42\t\n    43\t     ```\n    44\t     ⚠️ STA
CKED PR — base is `[parent-branch]`, not main.\n    45\t     After `[parent-bran
ch]` merges to main, run:\n    46\t       git rebase main && git push --force-wi
th-lease && gh pr edit --base main\n    47\t     before merging this PR.\n    48
\t     ```\n    49\t\n    50\t   - Print a terminal stop-note after PR creation:
\n    51\t\n    52\t     ```\n    53\t     ⚠️  STACKED PR: this PR targets [paren
t-branch], not main.\n    54\t         After [parent-branch] merges, rebase onto
main and update the base before merging.\n    55\t     ```\n    56\t\n    57\t  
- **Do not auto-rebase. Do not auto-update the base.** Both are irreversible and
can silently misresolve conflicts.\n    58\t\n    59\t3. **Run test suite** — un
it, integration, type-check, lint. Must all pass.\n    60\t4. **Coverage audit**
— check coverage didn\'t drop below threshold. Flag if it did.\n    61\t5. **Pla
n completion check** — verify all tasks in `docs/plans/{ticket}-plan.md` are add
ressed\n    62\t6. **Run `aet-review`** — staff-level code review on the diff\n 
  63\t7. **Run `aet-cso`** — security audit if the diff touches auth, data, API,
or dependencies\n    64\t8. **Split commits** — ensure each commit is bisectable
(one logical change). Split if needed.\n    65\t9. **Generate CHANGELOG** — add 
entry based on commit messages and plan.md summary\n    66\t10. **Bump VERSION**
— auto-bump patch. Stop for human decision on MINOR/MAJOR.\n    67\t11. **Push a
nd open PR** — push branch, create PR with description linking plan.md and PRD\n
