Overview\n     4\t\n     5\tAdd automatic merge verification to `aet-ship`, `aet
-pipeline-implement`, and `aet-work` to prevent the "Local Merge Trap" — a silen
t data-loss scenario where branches are deleted after being "merged" locally but
their commits never reach `origin/main`.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Goals\n     8\t\n
    9\t- `aet-ship` halts with a clear warning if `git merge-base --is-ancestor 
HEAD origin/main` fails before any branch deletion\n    10\t- `aet-pipeline-impl
ement` supports a `merged` stage after `synced` and updates the work queue with 
`merge_verified`\n    11\t- `aet-work` checks `merge_verified` on the previous t
ask before starting the next task\n    12\t- All three skills reference the same
verification command: `git merge-base --is-ancestor <ref> origin/main`\n    13\t
- Backward-compatible: old work queues without `merge_verified` are treated as u
nverified, not broken\n    14\t\n    15\t## Non-Goals\n    16\t\n    17\t- Do no
t add git hooks (rejected alternative — invisible to agents, bypassable)\n    18
\t- Do not create wrapper scripts or aliases (rejected alternative — user-local,
not agent-driven)\n    19\t- Do not retroactively detect dangling commits (rejec
ted alternative — detective, not preventive)\n    20\t- Do not modify runtime ap
plication source code; changes are limited to skill definitions (`SKILL.md` file
s)\n    21\t- Do not auto-merge PRs or modify remote repository state beyond ver
ification\n    22\t\n    23\t## User Stories\n    24\t\n    25\t- As an AET user
running `aet-ship`, I want the skill to verify my branch is actually on `origin/
main` before deleting it, so that I don\'t accidentally lose work.\n    26\t- As
an AET user running `aet-pipeline-implement`, I want the pipeline to distinguish
between "docs synced" and "merged to main," so that branch deletion only happens
when it\'s truly safe.\n    27\t- As an AET user running `aet-work` in AFK mode,
I want the queue to verify the previous task\'s merge status before starting the
next task, so that downstream tasks don\'t fail or re-implement code that isn\'t
on `main` yet.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Acceptance Criteria\n    30\t\n    31\t- [ 
] `aet-ship/SKILL.md` contains a merge verification step that runs `git merge-ba
se --is-ancestor HEAD origin/main` before branch deletion\n    32\t- [ ] `aet-sh
ip/SKILL.md` prints a clear, actionable warning and exits non-zero if the check 
fails\n    33\t- [ ] `aet-pipeline-implement/SKILL.md` defines a `merged` stage 
in its stage table\n    34\t- [ ] `aet-pipeline-implement/SKILL.md` includes pos
t-ship verification procedure that updates plan stage to `merged` and work queue
`merge_verified` on success\n    35\t- [ ] `aet-work/SKILL.md` adds `merge_verif
ied` and `merge_commit` fields to work queue schema\n    36\t- [ ] `aet-work/SKI
LL.md` checks the previous task\'s `merge_verified` field before starting the ne
xt task\n    37\t- [ ] Old work queues without `merge_verified` continue to func
tion (treated as unverified, not broken)\n    38\t- [ ] All three updated `SKILL
.md` files remain under 400 lines\n    39\t- [ ] `make validate` passes after al
l changes\n    40\t- [ ] `make package` regenerates all `.skill` files without e
rrors\n    41\t\n    42\t## Technical Notes\n    43\t\n    44\t- Verification co
mmand to use across all skills: `git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD origin/main`\
n    45\t- The `merged` stage in `aet-pipeline-implement` sits after `synced` in
the progression: `synced` → `merged`\n    46\t- `aet-work` work-queue JSON schem
a addition is additive; existing queues without the field are gracefully handled
\n    47\t- Each skill change is independent enough to be its own plan, but orde
red by dependency: `aet-ship` first, then `aet-pipeline-implement`, then `aet-wo
rk`\n    48\t- Changes are documentation-only (SKILL.md updates) — no applicatio
n runtime code is modified\n    49\t- An ADR should document why toolkit-level e
nforcement is preferred over project-level `AGENTS.md` rules\n    50\t\n    51\t
## Risks\n    52\t\n    53\t| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |\n    54\
t|------|-----------|--------|------------|\n    55\t| SKILL.md line count excee
ds 400 | Medium | Low | Move deep detail to `references/`; the changes are ~20-2
5 lines per skill |\n    56\t| `git merge-base` behavior differs across git vers
ions | Low | Low | Use standard plumbing command available since git 1.5+ |\n   
57\t| Users on non-`main` default branches | Medium | Medium | Use `origin/main`
