        output='     1\t---\n     2\tname: aet-ship\n     3\tdescription: Pre-me
rge validation gate with bisectable commits, changelog generation, and PR creati
on. Use when code is reviewed and ready to merge. Fully non-interactive except f
or merge conflicts, test failures, and version bump decisions. Triggers on reque
sts like "ship this," "prepare PR," or "merge ready."\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n  
  6\t# aet-ship\n     7\t\n     8\tPre-merge validation for agentic engineering.
The final gate before code lands.\n     9\t\n    10\t## When to Use\n    11\t\n 
  12\t- Code has been implemented and reviewed\n    13\t- You\'re ready to open 
or update a PR\n    14\t- As the final step of the PIV loop\n    15\t\n    16\t#
# Shared Preamble\n    17\t\n    18\tBefore executing any command in this skill,
collect the following context:\n    19\t\n    20\t- `BRANCH` — current git branc
h\n    21\t- `REPO_STATE` — clean / dirty / merge-conflict\n    22\t- `AGENTS_MD
` — presence and last-modified date of AGENTS.md\n    23\t- `LEARNINGS` — top-3 
relevant entries from `.agents/learnings.jsonl` (if exists)\n    24\t- `ACTIVE_P
LAN` — any `docs/plans/*.md` modified in last 7 days\n    25\t- `LAST_PIV` — dat
e of last completed plan-implement-validate cycle (from git log if available)\n 
  26\t\n    27\tUse this context to ground all recommendations. Do not ask the u
ser to provide it manually.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Commands\n    30\t\n    31\t##
# `ship`\n    32\t\n    33\tRun the pre-merge validation gate.\n    34\t\n    35
\t**Procedure:**\n    36\t\n    37\t1. **Sync with main** — pull latest main, at
tempt trivial merge conflict resolution\n    38\t2. **Stacked branch detection**
— run `git merge-base HEAD main` and compare to `git rev-parse main`. If they di
ffer, the branch was not branched directly from main\'s current tip — treat as s
tacked.\n    39\t\n    40\t   - Identify the parent branch by scanning `git log 
--oneline --decorate main..HEAD` for the nearest named ancestor (the last commit
decorated with a non-HEAD, non-remote ref).\n    41\t   - Still create the PR ag
ainst the parent branch — that is correct at creation time.\n    42\t   - Prepen
d a `⚠️ STACKED PR` section to the PR body:\n    43\t\n    44\t     ```\n    45\t
    ⚠️ STACKED PR — base is `[parent-branch]`, not main.\n    46\t     After `[pa
rent-branch]` merges to main, run:\n    47\t       git rebase main && git push -
-force-with-lease && gh pr edit --base main\n    48\t     before merging this PR
.\n    49\t     ```\n    50\t\n    51\t   - Print a terminal stop-note after PR 
creation:\n    52\t\n    53\t     ```\n    54\t     ⚠️  STACKED PR: this PR targe
ts [parent-branch], not main.\n    55\t         After [parent-branch] merges, re
base onto main and update the base before merging.\n    56\t     ```\n    57\t\n
   58\t   - **Do not auto-rebase. Do not auto-update the base.** Both are irreve
rsible and can silently misresolve conflicts.\n    59\t\n    60\t3. **Run test s
uite** — unit, integration, type-check, lint. Must all pass.\n    61\t4. **Cover
age audit** — check coverage didn\'t drop below threshold. Flag if it did.\n    
62\t5. **Plan completion check** — verify all tasks in `docs/plans/{ticket}-plan
.md` are addressed\n    63\t6. **Run `aet-review`** — staff-level code review on
the diff\n    64\t7. **Run `aet-cso`** — security audit if the diff touches auth
, data, API, or dependencies\n    65\t8. **Split commits** — ensure each commit 
is bisectable (one logical change). Split if needed.\n    66\t9. **Generate CHAN
GELOG** — add entry based on commit messages and plan.md summary\n    67\t10. **
Bump VERSION** — auto-bump patch. Stop for human decision on MINOR/MAJOR.\n    6
