        output='     1\t---\n     2\tname: aet-work\n     3\tdescription: Work q
ueue management and sequential task execution. Use when you have plan.md files t
o run in order, want hands-free task execution, or need to check what\'s ready. 
Triggers on "run the queue", "pick next task", "what\'s next", "what\'s unblocke
d", "run all tasks", "keep working", "run tasks", "execute plans", "night shift"
, "AFK mode", "queue status", "init queue", "what can I work on", "run unblocked
tasks".\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# aet-work\n     7\t\n     8\tQueue mana
gement for agentic engineering. The single job of this skill is to manage the wo
rk queue and orchestrate task execution — not to plan, implement, or review.\n  
  9\t\n    10\t## When to Use\n    11\t\n    12\t- You have multiple `docs/plans
/*.md` files from a PRD breakdown\n    13\t- You want to run tasks sequentially 
without manual intervention\n    14\t- You want to check what\'s blocked, what\'
s unblocked, what\'s done\n    15\t- You want the "night shift" AFK loop\n    16
\t\n    17\t## Shared Preamble\n    18\t\n    19\tBefore executing any command i
n this skill, collect the following context:\n    20\t\n    21\t- `BRANCH` — cur
rent git branch\n    22\t- `REPO_STATE` — clean / dirty / merge-conflict\n    23
\t- `AGENTS_MD` — presence and last-modified date of AGENTS.md\n    24\t- `LEARN
INGS` — top-3 relevant entries from `.agents/learnings.jsonl` (if exists)\n    2
5\t- `ACTIVE_PLAN` — any `docs/plans/*.md` modified in last 7 days\n    26\t- `L
AST_PIV` — date of last completed plan-implement-validate cycle (from git log if
available)\n    27\t- `ACTIVE_PRD_STAGE` — current `*Stage:` value from the most
-recently-modified `docs/prds/*.md` footer (if exists)\n    28\t- `ACTIVE_PLAN_S
TAGE` — current `*Stage:` value from the most-recently-modified `docs/plans/*.md
` footer (if exists)\n    29\t\n    30\tUse this context to ground all recommend
ations. Do not ask the user to provide it manually.\n    31\t\n    32\tIf a stag
e is found, print at the start of execution: `"📍 Current stage: {stage}."`\n   
33\t\n    34\t## Commands\n    35\t\n    36\t### `init-queue`\n    37\t\n    38\
tRead all `docs/plans/*.md` and produce `.agents/work-queue.json`.\n    39\t\n  
 40\t**Procedure:**\n    41\t\n    42\t1. Scan `docs/plans/` for all `*.md` file
s\n    43\t2. For each plan.md, extract: title, task ID (from filename or frontm
atter), blocking relationships\n    44\t3. Build the DAG using `blocks` and `blo
cked_by` arrays\n    45\t4. Set initial status: `unblocked` if `blocked_by` is e
mpty, `blocked` otherwise\n    46\t5. Set `merge_verified: false` and `merge_com
mit: null` on each entry\n    47\t6. Set `source_prd` to the most recent PRD in 
`docs/prds/` (if any)\n    48\t7. Write `.agents/work-queue.json`\n    49\t\n   
50\t### `status`\n    51\t\n    52\tShow the current state of the work queue.\n 
  53\t\n    54\t**Procedure:**\n    55\t\n    56\t1. Read `.agents/work-queue.js
on`\n    57\t2. Report counts: unblocked, blocked, in-progress, done, failed\n  
 58\t3. List the next 3 unblocked tasks (topological order)\n    59\t4. List any
failed tasks (require human attention)\n    60\t\n    61\t### `next`\n    62\t\n
   63\tIdentify and output the next unblocked task.\n    64\t\n    65\t**Procedu
re:**\n    66\t\n    67\t1. Read `.agents/work-queue.json`\n    68\t2. Find task
s with `status: "unblocked"`\n    69\t3. Pick the first in topological order (re
specting the DAG)\n    70\t4. Output: task ID, title, plan_file path\n    71\t5.
Update status to `in-progress` in the queue file\n    72\t\n    73\t### `run`\n 
  74\t\n    75\tAFK loop: implement tasks until none remain or a failure occurs.
\n    76\t\n    77\t**Procedure:**\n    78\t\n    79\t```\n    80\twhile true:\n
   81\t  1. Read .agents/work-queue.json\n    82\t  2. Find next unblocked task\
n    83\t  3. If no unblocked tasks remain:\n    84\t     - Report completion; l
ist all task branches created\n    85\t     - Break loop\n    86\t  4. Mark task
as in-progress in queue\n    87\t  5. Merge verification: for each task in this 
task\'s `blocked_by` list,\n    88\t     read its entry from `.agents/work-queue
.json`.\n    89\t     - If `merge_verified` is `true`: continue silently\n    90
\t     - If `merge_verified` is `false` or missing: print\n    91\t       "⚠️  Wa
