ed` is treated as unverified, not broken.\n    94\t  6. Create a worktree for th
e task (ensure .worktrees/ is in .gitignore):\n    95\t       git worktree add .
worktrees/<task-id> -b <task-id>\n    96\t     Resume case: if the task is alrea
dy in-progress and .worktrees/<task-id> exists,\n    97\t     skip this step — t
he worktree from the interrupted session is still valid.\n    98\t  6. CLEAR CON
TEXT — request a new session or context reset.\n    99\t     This is cooperative
isolation: it works when the agent supports `/clear`,\n   100\t     session rest
art, or equivalent. If the runtime does not support mid-session\n   101\t     re
sets, use `run-scripted` instead for guaranteed OS-process isolation.\n   102\t 
   The queue file persists state; resume by running aet-work run again.\n   103\
t  8. Load minimal context: AGENTS.md + last 5 commits + current branch\n   104\
t  9. cd into .worktrees/<task-id>; read the task\'s plan.md\n   105\t  10. Run 
`aet-pipeline-implement` on the task\'s plan.md (this handles the full quality\n
  106\t     pipeline: tdd → implement → qa → review → cso → sync-docs; worktree 
is already\n   107\t     created, so skip the worktree setup step inside the pip
eline)\n   108\t  11. If `aet-pipeline-implement` stops at any gate (validation 
failure, architecture\n   109\t      issue, security finding, or any hard-stop c
ondition):\n   110\t      - cd back to repo root\n   111\t      - Mark task as f
ailed in queue; record which stage it stopped at\n   112\t      - Stop loop, rep
ort failure (branch preserved at .worktrees/<task-id>)\n   113\t  12. cd back to
repo root (aet-pipeline-implement commits atomically per step;\n   114\t      al
l changes are already committed by the time the pipeline finishes)\n   115\t  13
. Mark task as done; record branch name (<task-id>) in queue entry\n   116\t  14
. Update dependent tasks: if all blocked_by are done, set to unblocked\n   117\t
 15. CLEAR CONTEXT again before the next iteration.\n   118\t      If context cl
earing is not reliable in this runtime, switch to\n   119\t      `run-scripted` 
for guaranteed isolation.\n   120\t```\n   121\t\n   122\t**Human-in-the-loop ga
tes:**\n   123\t\n   124\t- Loop stops on validation failure\n   125\t- Loop sto
ps on review failure\n   126\t- Loop stops on merge conflicts\n   127\t- Loop ca
n be run with `--dry-run` to preview only (no implementation)\n   128\t- Loop ne
ver auto-ships; aet-ship is a separate human-triggered step\n   129\t\n   130\t*
*Context isolation details:**\n   131\t\n   132\t- Context window: cleared betwe
en tasks by starting a new session (works in every agent)\n   133\t- Branch isol
ation: each task gets its own branch at `.worktrees/<task-id>/`\n   134\t- State
persistence: `.agents/work-queue.json` survives context resets — it is the\n   1
35\t  handoff between sessions, not memory\n   136\t- After the loop: N branches
ready for independent review; `git worktree list` shows all\n   137\t\n   138\t#
## `run-scripted`\n   139\t\n   140\tAFK loop with OS-level process isolation. G
enerates a bash orchestrator script tailored to the detected agent CLI, spawns i
t as a background OS process, and waits for completion. Each task executes in a 
fresh agent process with its own git worktree, eliminating context leakage and b
ranch overlap entirely.\n   141\t\n   142\t**When to use instead of `run`:**\n  
